# Vir Das: Landing — 6 Key Scenes

Scenes are copied word for word from the transcript in [[Vir Das Transcript_ Landing, by Vir Das (2022)]], with line breaks tidied. Check them against the recorded special, since transcripts can differ from the performance.

**Field of inquiry:** Politics, power and justice / Beliefs, values and education  
**Global issue:** Free speech and state/media backlash against an artist's criticism of his nation  
**Techniques:** Frame narrative setting up a later callback, Ironic reversal (the video about duality divides the nation), Imagined act-out of offended terrorists, Absurd exaggeration  
**Context:** Early in the special, Das frames the show as a flight home to possible arrest and recounts the sedition complaints, "terrorist" headlines and media storm after his Two Indias monologue.
  
**Content note:** Some strong language; jokes about terrorism and ISIS.

> [!quote] 1. The Air India Flight and the "Two Indias" Backlash
